      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "Blue shark (<i>Prionace glauca</i>), Faial-Pico Channel, Azores Islands, Portugal. The blue shark is a species of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/requiem_shark\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:requiem shark\">requiem shark</a>, in the family Carcharhinidae, that inhabits deep waters (images taken though between 5 and 10 meter below water) averaging around 3.1 m (10 ft) and preferring cooler waters. They can live up to 20 years, can move very quickly and feed primarily on small <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Fish\" title=\"Fish\">fish</a> and <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Squid\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Squid\">squid</a>, although they can take larger prey.",
